  "description": "Startup Street XI is a 24-hour entrepreneurial marathon that takes participants through the startup journey — from ideation and market validation to business planning and pitching . With expert mentors, industry speakers, networking opportunities, and a Shark Tank-style final pitch, participants get hands-on exposure to real-world entrepreneurship. Event Timeline: Day 1 – Kickoff & Ideation 5:00 PM – 6:00 PM: Registration & Check-in 6:00 PM – 6:30 PM: Opening Ceremony & Briefing 6:30 PM – 7:30 PM: Speaker Session & Q&A 7:30 PM – 8:00 PM: Team Formation & Networking 8:00 PM – 10:00 PM: Ideation & Problem Validation 10:00 PM – 11:00 PM: Mentor Checkpoint 11:00 PM – 12:00 AM: Engagement Activities 12:00 AM – 8:00 AM: Overnight Preparation Day 2 – Review & Pitching 8:30 AM – 9:30 AM: Review Round 1 9:30 AM – 10:30 AM: Speaker Session & Q&A 10:45 AM – 11:00 AM: Elimination Round 11:15 AM – 1:00 PM: Pitching Round 1 1:00 PM – 2:00 PM: Lunch & Networking 2:00 PM – 4:00 PM: Final Pitching Round 4:00 PM – 4:30 PM: Valedictory & Prize Distribution Key Highlights: 24-hour overnight entrepreneurial challenge Mentorship from industry experts Market research and business model development Networking and speaker sessions Shark Tank-style pitching Opportunity to transform ideas into actionable ventures",
